            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 1: Author Background and Authority"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Michelle LaVaughn Robinson Obama is the daughter of Fraser Robinson III and Marian Robinson, raised in a working-class family on the South Side of Chicago in a small apartment above her great-aunt Robbie Shields.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c002",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 2: The Central Problem"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The book addresses the struggle of navigating life's transitions while maintaining authenticity and purpose. The central problem is the tension between external expectations (societal, political, familial) and internal growth, the challenge of \"becoming\" when the world wants to define you as already complete.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c003",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 3: The Root Cause of Human Struggle"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The root cause is the belief in a fixed identity, the notion that one can \"become something and that's the end,\" coupled with the internalization of external judgments that limit self-perception.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c004",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 4: The Complete Methodology - Every Step"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "While \"Becoming\" is a memoir, the methodology for personal growth and professional execution can be extracted as follows: The Personal Evolution Framework: 1.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c005",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 5: Non-Negotiable Principles"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "- Truth-Telling: \"I tried to communicate the one message... that I knew invisibility... I came from a history of invisibility.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c006",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 6: The Transformation Arc"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Before the Methodology: The \"box-checker\", meticulous, perfectionist, anxious, controlling every detail. She describes herself as having \"lived like a half-closeted CEO, quietly but unswervingly focused on achievement, bent on checking every box.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c007",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 7: Coaching Questions"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "- \"What kind of person do I want to be? How do I want to contribute to the world?\" (From her 1991 journal) - \"Am I good enough?",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c008",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 8: Tools, Exercises, and Practices"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The Journal Practice: Kept a \"clothbound black book with purple flowers on the cover\" starting in 1991. Used to \"sort through my jumbled feelings\" and answer: \"What kind of person do I want to be?",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c009",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 9: Objection Handling and Resistance"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "To the \"Angry Black Woman\" Stereotype: \"I wanted to ask my detractors which part of that phrase matters to them the most, is it 'angry' or 'black' or 'woman'?",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c010",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 10: Author Voice and Language"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Signature Phrases: - \"Becoming\" (as continuous verb) - \"The box-checker\" vs. \"the swerve\" - \"The gaze\" (referring to public scrutiny) - \"The bubble\" (referring to White House isolation) - \"When they go low, we go high\" - \"Am I good enough?",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c012",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 12: The Repeatable Execution System"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "For High-Stakes Public Leadership: 1. Deep Research Phase: \"I was realizing that the next phase of my journey would not simply unfold on its own...",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c013",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 13: The Quality Bar"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Excellent execution, according to this methodology, produces: - Measurable Community Impact: Not just \"awareness\" but concrete results, \"45 million kids eating healthier breakfasts and lunches,\" \"1.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-michelle-obama-becoming-c014",
          "source_id": "src-michelle-obama-becoming",
          "source_version": "e264bffae8e88954fb6adc830caa8526a72a910e6b18570684d5a758d6d2a3dc",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 14: Non-Negotiable Execution Rules"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "- Never Skip Preparation: \"I could see how the opposition had managed to dice up these images and feed me to the public as some sort of pissed-off harpy\", she learned to prepare for optics as well as content.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "michelle-obama"
        },
        {
